Last updated: 2026-11-09.

This page describes how the personal assistant "Hermes Agent", operated by Jordi Bru Carci on a private server, uses data from Google APIs.

## Data accessed

With the permissions the user grants during OAuth, the assistant can read Gmail messages and Google Calendar events belonging to the user's own Google account, and create or modify them only when the user explicitly asks.

## Use of data

Data is used only to answer the user's requests and to produce summaries for the user. It is not used for advertising, profiling, or training of AI models.

## Storage

OAuth tokens and retrieved data are stored only on the operator's private server, with access limited to the operator. Data is not sold, shared with third parties, or transferred to anyone else, except as required by law.

## Limited Use

The use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.

## Revoking access

You can revoke access at any time at https://myaccount.google.com/permissions or by contacting the operator.

## Contact

Jordi Bru Carci: jordibru00@gmail.com

